  "fps": 12,
  "about": [
    "TAB-1 on the title screen. Separate from `tab-1/rig/clips.json`, which is",
    "the COMBAT vocabulary — hurt, hack, beaten, cheer, hit. Nothing in there is",
    "usable here: those clips are 0.6-2.4s and they read as reactions, because a",
    "reaction is what a fight needs. A title screen is the opposite problem. The",
    "player is not doing anything and may be sitting on this frame for minutes,",
    "so every clip here is 7-11 seconds, most of it spent HOLDING.",
    "",
    "── The rule that makes sequencing free ─────────────────────────────────",
    "",
    "Every clip starts at the rest pose and ends at the rest pose. Nothing eases",
    "across a boundary, nothing blends, and the director can therefore cut from",
    "any clip to any other clip on any frame without a transition — the two poses",
    "either side of the cut are identical. Cut-out animation cannot crossfade",
    "anyway: paper does not dissolve.",
    "",
    "── Why they are so slow ────────────────────────────────────────────────",
    "",
    "The temptation is a one-second wobble that snaps back, and it is wrong twice:",
    "it reads as a loop the moment you have seen it twice, and it makes the",
    "character look nervous. What sells a small paper robot standing alone in a",
    "room is the HOLD — the four seconds it spends looking into the slot without",
    "moving. So most keys here are far apart, and each clip has exactly one idea:",
    "",
    "  idle-breathe   the baseline. Almost nothing. A weight settle you notice",
    "                 only if you watch for it.",
    "  idle-look      turns its head down the corridor, holds a long beat, comes",
    "                 back. The hold is the whole clip.",
    "  idle-shift     unweights one leg, leans, and takes its time coming back.",
    "                 The only clip that touches the legs while standing.",
    "  idle-peer      leans out over the slot and looks into it. The story beat:",
    "                 this is the shredder, and it is looking in.",
    "  idle-check     lifts one arm, pauses as if reading it, lowers it. The one",
    "                 clip with a deliberate, legible action.",
    "  walk           a slow four-beat cycle, meant to be looped by the director",
    "                 while it also translates the whole rig sideways.",
    "",
    "Arms rest at -7 and +7 degrees, so an arm track that wants to hang straight",
    "goes to +7 / -7, not to 0."
  ],
